    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nThe acceptance tests read `membershipTier` off `GET /api/owners/{id}`, whose response is an `OwnerDto` produced by `OwnerMapper` from the `Owner` entity. I added the derived field there:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits the field/getter/setter on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` plus a `membershipTier(Owner)` helper implementing the rule:\n   - `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank);\n   - `BRONZE` otherwise (including when `namesakeCount` is null).\n\n`namesakeCount` is already populated on create by the existing `CountOwnerNamesakes` pipeline step, so the tier is correct both at create time and on subsequent GETs. No new endpoint/YAML was needed since the derivation is a pure function of the owner's own fields.\n\n## Tests\n- `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique owner + email \u2192 SILVER) \u2705\n- `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE) \u2705\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
